*Steps to Reproduce:*
 *  Open AEM guides XML Editor.
 * From Setting, click on Spellcheck
 * observe the POST call

There is a requirement from Swift to be able to run AEM guides Spellcheck on EN_GB language.
 * On analysis of spellcheck, we found that the servlet called for spellcheck functionality doesn't pass any language parameter.              {color:#0747a6}_[/libs/cq/ui/rte/spellcheck|http://localhost:4504/libs/cq/ui/rte/spellcheck]_{color} 
 * On checking class SpellCheckServlet, it was observed that language is not passed in the Post API and the servlet is expecting a language parameter.            

{color:#0747a6}              _String language = req.getParameter(LANGUAGE);_{color}
 * Hence, the default language EN_US seems to be taking affect.

              {color:#0747a6}_public static final String DEFAULT_LANGUAGE = "en_us";_{color}

{color:#0747a6}              _language = DEFAULT_LANGUAGE;_{color}

 

+*Expectation:*+

The customer should be able to choose language for which they want to run spellcheck

When the user presses the Enter key while the focus is in a table cell within a text (which is not enclosed in a {*}<p></p>{*}), a new empty *<p></p>* element is appended to the end of the text instead of splitting the paragraph at the cursor position.

To fix:
 * If the cursor position is in a table cell inside a text string (which is the direct child of {*}<entry>{*}) and the user presses the Enter key, the text before the cursor position should be wrapped in {*}<p></p>{*}, and the text string after the cursor position should also be wrapped in {*}<p></p>{*}.

Example - Before:
{code:xml}
<entry>This is sentence 1. This is sentence 2.</entry>{code}
Now user sets the text insertion mark between the two sentences and hits Return.

Expected Result:
{code:xml}
<entry>
   <p>This is sentence 1.</p>
   <p>This is sentence 2.</p>
</entry>{code}
We should additionally remove leading and trailing spaces in the PCDATA. That is, we should clean up something like this:
{code:xml}
<p> This is sentence 1.  </p>{code}
To this:
{code:xml}
<p>This is sentence 1.</p>{code}

